# Security

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), the single source of repository instructions.

- No `eval`, `new Function`, or dynamic imports/requires of user-supplied strings.
  Conditions are names resolved by a registry, never code to evaluate.
- Only llm-gateway imports provider SDKs. Validate external data before use, with Zod at
  TypeScript boundaries and typed validation in native code.
- Secrets come only from environment variables. Never include secrets or PII in logs or tests;
  use synthetic fixtures. Keep credentials out of code, definitions, prompts, and artifacts.
- Preserve redaction and `noLog` behavior; do not log full model prompts or completions.
- Delimit untrusted prompt content from system instructions; treat model/tool output as data.
- Enforce tool permission declarations and explicit allow-listing of sensitive capabilities.
  Sensitive actions pass through approval gates. Agents cannot approve their own outputs.
- Follow SECURITY.md for reporting vulnerabilities. Security-sensitive structural changes
  require maintainer review under CONTRIBUTING.md.
